'''Alignment restrictions:''' none

'''[[Hit die]]:''' d10

'''Proficiencies:''' armor ([[armor proficiency (light)|light]], [[armor proficiency (medium)|medium]]), weapons ([[weapon proficiency (martial)|martial]], [[weapon proficiency (simple)|simple]])

'''[[Skill point]]s:''' 4 + intelligence modifier

'''Skills:'''  [[craft armor]], [[craft trap]], [[craft weapon]], [[heal (skill)|heal]], [[intimidate]], [[jump]], [[lore]], [[perform]], [[spot]], [[tumble]]

'''Primary saving throw(s):''' [[fortitude]]

==Special abilities & feats==
*Level 1 brawler fists (1d6), bonus feat, [[improved unarmed strike]]
*Level 4 bonus feat
*Level 6 brawler fists (1d8, +1 enhancement)
*Level 8 bonus feat
*Level 12 brawler fists (1d10, +2 enhancement)
*Level 16 bonus feat
*Level 18 brawler fists (2d6, +3 enhancement)
*Level 20 bonus feat


'''Bonus feats:''' [[ambidexterity]], [[blind fight]], [[called shot]], [[cleave]], [[deflect arrows]], [[disarm]], [[dodge]], [[expertise]], [[great cleave]], [[improved critical]], [[improved disarm]], [[improved expertise]], [[improved knockdown]],  [[improved parry]], [[improved power attack]], [[improved two-weapon fighting]], [[improved unarmed strike]], [[knockdown]], [[power attack]], [[rapid shot]], [[spring attack]],  [[stunning fist]],  [[two-weapon fighting]], [[weapon finesse]], [[weapon focus]], [[weapon proficiency (exotic)]], [[mobility]], [[point blank shot]],  [[whirlwind attack]], [[great fortitude]], [[iron will]], [[lightning reflexes]]

'''Special:''' Brawler fists: A brawler's fists do more damage than a normal character's, but only when fighting without weapons or a shield. In addition, the strengthening of the flesh and bone of the hand caused by constantly punching hard things has given them the ability to pierce through [[damage reduction]], starting at level 6.

==Notes==
*Added in the [[PRC Expansion Pack]].
*If multiclassed with a [[monk]], the character will use whichever unarmed damage is better. It does not stack. In addition, taking a level in monk disables the use of certain brawler bonus feats.

